.SS sep.Background
.SS sep.extract
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B sep.extract(data, thresh, err=None, mask=None, minarea=5, filter_kernel=default_kernel, filter_type=\(aqmatched\(aq, deblend_nthresh=32, deblend_cont=0.005, clean=True, clean_param=1.0, segmentation_map=False)
Extract sources from an image.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBdata\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
Data array (2\-d).
.TP
\fBthresh\fP (float)
Threshold pixel value for detection. If an \fBerr\fP or \fBvar\fP array
is not given, this is interpreted as an absolute threshold. If \fBerr\fP
or \fBvar\fP is given, this is interpreted as a relative threshold: the
absolute threshold at pixel (j, i) will be \fBthresh * err[j, i]\fP or
\fBthresh * sqrt(var[j, i])\fP\&.
.TP
\fBerr, var\fP (float or \fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
Error \fIor\fP variance (specify at most one). This can be used to
specify a pixel\-by\-pixel detection threshold; see \(dqthresh\(dq argument.
.TP
\fBgain\fP (float, optional)
Conversion factor between data array units and poisson counts. This
does not affect detection; it is used only in calculating Poisson
noise contribution to uncertainty parameters such as \fBerrx2\fP\&. If
not given, no Poisson noise will be added.
.TP
\fBmask\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
Mask array. \fBTrue\fP values, or numeric values greater than
\fBmaskthresh\fP, are considered masked. Masking a pixel is equivalent
to setting data to zero and noise (if present) to infinity, and occurs
\fIbefore\fP filtering.
.TP
\fBmaskthresh\fP (float, optional)
Threshold for a pixel to be masked. Default is \fB0.0\fP\&.
.TP
\fBminarea\fP (int, optional)
Minimum number of pixels required for an object. Default is 5.
.TP
\fBfilter_kernel\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray> or None, optional)
Filter kernel used for on\-the\-fly filtering (used to
enhance detection). Default is a 3x3 array:
[[1,2,1], [2,4,2], [1,2,1]]. Set to \fBNone\fP to skip
convolution.
.TP
\fBfilter_type\fP ({\(aqmatched\(aq, \(aqconv\(aq}, optional)
Filter treatment. This affects filtering behavior when a noise
array is supplied. \fB\(aqmatched\(aq\fP (default) accounts for
pixel\-to\-pixel noise in the filter kernel. \fB\(aqconv\(aq\fP is
simple convolution of the data array, ignoring pixel\-to\-pixel
noise across the kernel.  \fB\(aqmatched\(aq\fP should yield better
detection of faint sources in areas of rapidly varying noise
(such as found in coadded images made from semi\-overlapping
exposures).  The two options are equivalent when noise is
constant.
.TP
\fBdeblend_nthresh\fP (int, optional)
Number of thresholds used for object deblending. Default is 32.
.TP
\fBdeblend_cont\fP (float, optional)
Minimum contrast ratio used for object deblending. Default is 0.005.
To entirely disable deblending, set to 1.0.
.TP
\fBclean\fP (bool, optional)
Perform cleaning? Default is True.
.TP
\fBclean_param\fP (float, optional)
Cleaning parameter (see SExtractor manual). Default is 1.0.
.TP
\fBsegmentation_map\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray> or bool, optional)
If \fBTrue\fP, also return a \(dqsegmentation map\(dq giving the member
pixels of each object. Default is False.
.sp
\fINew in v1.3.0\fP:
An existing segmentation map can also be supplied in
the form of an \fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>\&. If this is the case, then the
object detection stage is skipped, and the objects in the
segmentation map are analysed and extracted.
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B Returns
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBobjects\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
Extracted object parameters (structured array). Available fields are:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBthresh\fP (float) Threshold at object location.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnpix\fP (int) Number of pixels belonging to the object.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtnpix\fP (int) Number of pixels above threshold (unconvolved data).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBxmin\fP, \fBxmax\fP (int) Minimum, maximum x coordinates of pixels.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBymin\fP, \fBymax\fP (int) Minimum, maximum y coordinates of pixels.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBx\fP, \fBy\fP (float) object barycenter (first moments).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBx2\fP, \fBy2\fP, \fBxy\fP (float) Second moments.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBerrx2\fP, \fBerry2\fP, \fBerrxy\fP (float) Second moment errors.
Note that these will be zero if error is not given.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBa\fP, \fBb\fP, \fBtheta\fP (float) Ellipse parameters, scaled as
described by Section 8.4.2 in \(dqThe Source Extractor Guide\(dq or
Section 10.1.5\-6 of v2.13 of SExtractor\(aqs User Manual.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcxx\fP, \fBcyy\fP, \fBcxy\fP (float) Alternative ellipse parameters.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcflux\fP (float) Sum of member pixels in convolved data.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBflux\fP (float) Sum of member pixels in unconvolved data.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcpeak\fP (float) Peak value in convolved data.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpeak\fP (float) Peak value in unconvolved data.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBxcpeak\fP, \fBycpeak\fP (int) Coordinate of convolved peak pixel.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBxpeak\fP, \fBypeak\fP (int) Coordinate of unconvolved peak pixel.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBflag\fP (int) Extraction flags.
.UNINDENT
.TP
\fBsegmap\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
Array of integers with same shape as data. Pixels not belonging to
any object have value 0. All pixels belonging to the \fBi\fP\-th object
(e.g., \fBobjects[i]\fP) have value \fBi+1\fP\&. Only returned if
\fBsegmentation_map = True | ~numpy.ndarray\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
