.SS sep.sum_circle
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B sep.sum_circle(data, x, y, r, err=None, var=None, mask=None, maskthresh=0.0, segmap=None, seg_id=None, bkgann=None, gain=None, subpix=5)
Sum data in circular aperture(s).
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBdata\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
2\-d array to be summed.
.TP
\fBx, y, r\fP (array_like)
Center coordinates and radius (radii) of aperture(s).
\fBx\fP corresponds to the second (\(dqfast\(dq) axis of the input array
and \fBy\fP corresponds to the first (\(dqslow\(dq) axis.
\fBx, y = (0.0, 0.0)\fP corresponds to the center of the first
element of the array. These inputs obey numpy broadcasting rules.
.TP
\fBerr, var\fP (float or \fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
Error \fIor\fP variance (specify at most one).
.TP
\fBmask\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
Mask array. If supplied, a given pixel is masked if its value
is greater than \fBmaskthresh\fP\&.
.TP
\fBmaskthresh\fP (float, optional)
Threshold for a pixel to be masked. Default is \fB0.0\fP\&.
.TP
\fBsegmap\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
Segmentation image with dimensions of \fBdata\fP and dtype \fBnp.int32\fP\&.
This is an optional input and corresponds to the segmentation map
output by \fBextract\fP \%<#\:sep\:.extract>\&.
.TP
\fBseg_id\fP (array_like, optional)
Array of segmentation ids used to mask additional pixels in the image.
Dimensions correspond to the dimensions of \fBx\fP and \fBy\fP\&. The
behavior differs depending on whether \fBseg_id\fP is negative or
positive. If \fBseg_id\fP is positive, all pixels belonging to other
objects are masked. (Pixel \fBj, i\fP is masked if \fBseg[j, i] != seg_id
and seg[j, i] != 0\fP). If \fBseg_id\fP is negative, all pixels other
than those belonging to the object of interest are masked. (Pixel \fBj,
i\fP is masked if \fBseg[j, i] != \-seg_id\fP).  NB: must be included if
\fBsegmap\fP is provided.
.TP
\fBbkgann\fP (tuple, optional)
Length 2 tuple giving the inner and outer radius of a
\(dqbackground annulus\(dq. If supplied, the background is estimated
by averaging unmasked pixels in this annulus. If supplied, the inner
and outer radii obey numpy broadcasting rules along with \fBx\fP,
\fBy\fP and \fBr\fP\&.
.TP
\fBgain\fP (float, optional)
Conversion factor between data array units and poisson counts,
used in calculating poisson noise in aperture sum. If \fBNone\fP
(default), do not add poisson noise.
.TP
\fBsubpix\fP (int, optional)
Subpixel sampling factor. If 0, exact overlap is calculated.
