.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B sep.kron_radius(data, x, y, a, b, theta, r, mask=None, maskthresh=0.0, seg_id=None, segmap=None)
Calculate Kron \(dqradius\(dq within an ellipse.
.sp
The Kron radius is given by
.sp
.ce
\esum_i r_i I(r_i) / \esum_i I(r_i)
.ce 0
.sp
where the sum is over all pixels in the aperture and the radius is given
in units of \fBa\fP and \fBb\fP: \fBr_i\fP is the distance to the pixel relative
to the distance to the ellipse specified by \fBa\fP, \fBb\fP, \fBtheta\fP\&.
Equivalently, after converting the ellipse parameters to their coefficient
representation, \fBr_i\fP is given by
.sp
.ce
r_i^2 = cxx(x_i \- x)^2 + cyy(y_i \- y)^2 + cxx(x_i \- x)(y_i \- y)
.ce 0
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBdata\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
Data array.
.TP
\fBx, y\fP (array_like)
Ellipse center(s).
.TP
\fBa, b, theta\fP (array_like)
Ellipse parameters.
.TP
\fBr\fP (array_like)
\(dqRadius\(dq of ellipse over which to integrate. If the ellipse
extent correponds to second moments of an object, this is the
number of \(dqisophotal radii\(dq in Source Extractor parlance. A
Fixed value of 6 is used in Source Extractor.
.TP
\fBmask\fP (\fBnumpy.ndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
An optional mask.
.TP
\fBmaskthresh\fP (float, optional)
Pixels with mask > maskthresh will be ignored.
.TP
\fBsegmap\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
Segmentation image with dimensions of \fBdata\fP and dtype \fBnp.int32\fP\&.
This is an optional input and corresponds to the segmentation map
output by \fBextract\fP \%<#\:sep\:.extract>\&.
.TP
\fBseg_id\fP (array_like, optional)
Array of segmentation ids used to mask additional pixels in the image.
Dimensions correspond to the dimensions of \fBx\fP and \fBy\fP\&. The
behavior differs depending on whether \fBseg_id\fP is negative or
positive. If \fBseg_id\fP is positive, all pixels belonging to other
objects are masked. (Pixel \fBj, i\fP is masked if \fBseg[j, i] != seg_id
and seg[j, i] != 0\fP). If \fBseg_id\fP is negative, all pixels other
than those belonging to the object of interest are masked. (Pixel \fBj,
i\fP is masked if \fBseg[j, i] != \-seg_id\fP).  NB: must be included if
\fBsegmap\fP is provided.
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B Returns
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBkronrad\fP (array_like)
The Kron radius.
.TP
\fBflag\fP (array_like)
Integer value indicating conditions about the aperture or how
many masked pixels it contains.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
