.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B sep.winpos(data, xinit, yinit, sig, mask=None, maskthresh=0.0, subpix=11, minsig=2.0 / 2.35 * 0.5)
Calculate more accurate object centroids using \(aqwindowed\(aq algorithm.
.sp
Starting from the supplied initial center position, an iterative
algorithm is used to determine a better object centroid. On each
iteration, the centroid is calculated using all pixels within a
circular aperture of \fB4*sig\fP from the current position,
weighting pixel positions by their flux and the amplitude of a 2\-d
Gaussian with sigma \fBsig\fP\&. Iteration stops when the change in
position falls under some threshold or a maximum number of
iterations is reached. This is equivalent to \fBXWIN_IMAGE\fP and
\fBYWIN_IMAGE\fP parameters in Source Extractor (for the correct choice
of sigma for each object).
.sp
\fBNote:\fP One should be cautious about using windowed positions in
crowded fields or for sources with nearby neighbors, as the iterative
algorithm can fail catastrophically.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBdata\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
Data array.
.TP
\fBxinit, yinit\fP (array_like)
Initial center(s).
.TP
\fBsig\fP (array_like)
Gaussian sigma used for weighting pixels. Pixels within a circular
aperture of radius 4*sig are included.
.TP
\fBmask\fP (\fBnumpy.ndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>, optional)
An optional mask.
.TP
\fBmaskthresh\fP (float, optional)
Pixels with mask > maskthresh will be ignored.
.TP
\fBsubpix\fP (int, optional)
Subpixel sampling used to determine pixel overlap with
aperture.  11 is used in Source Extractor. For exact overlap
calculation, use 0.
.TP
\fBminsig\fP (float, optional)
Minimum bound on \fBsig\fP parameter. \fBsig\fP values smaller than this
are increased to \fBminsig\fP to replicate Source Extractor behavior.
Source Extractor uses a minimum half\-light radius of 0.5 pixels,
equivalent to a sigma of 0.5 * 2.0 / 2.35.
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B Returns
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBx, y\fP (np.ndarray)
New x and y position(s).
.TP
\fBflag\fP (np.ndarray)
Flags.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS sep.mask_ellipse
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B sep.mask_ellipse(arr, x, y, a, b, theta, r=1.0)
Mask ellipse(s) in an array.
.sp
Set array elements to True (or 1) if they fall within the given
ellipse.  The \fBr\fP keyword can be used to scale the ellipse.
Equivalently, after converting \fBa\fP, \fBb\fP, \fBtheta\fP to a
coefficient ellipse representation (\fBcxx\fP, \fBcyy\fP, \fBcxy\fP),
pixels that fulfill the condition
.sp
.ce
cxx(x_i \- x)^2 + cyy(y_i \- y)^2 + cxx(x_i \- x)(y_i \- y) < r^2
.ce 0
.sp
will be masked.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
\fBarr\fP (\fBndarray\fP \%<https://\:numpy\:.org/\:doc/\:stable/\:reference/\:generated/\:numpy\:.ndarray\:.html#\:numpy\:.ndarray>)
Input array to be masked. Array is updated in\-place.
.TP
\fBx, y\fP (array_like)
Center of ellipse(s).
.TP
\fBa, b, theta\fP (array_like, optional)
Parameters defining the extent of the ellipe(s).
.TP
\fBcxx, cyy, cxy\fP (array_like, optional)
Alternative ellipse representation. Can be used as
\fBmask_ellipse(arr, x, y, cxx=..., cyy=..., cxy=...)\fP\&.
.TP
\fBr\fP (array_like, optional)
Scale factor of ellipse(s). Default is 1.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS sep.ellipse_axes
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
